  const from = [];
  // ⛔ #a-province-turned-to-water-leaves-no-history-behind — EVERY DATE, NOT THE FIRST BUILDINGS BLOCK.
  //
  // This ran removeVictoryPointForProvince and removeProvinceBuildingBlock, and the second reads the FIRST `buildings`
  // block only. So what the state's history writes for the province in a date stayed behind, naming a province the
  // state no longer lists: vanilla 137-Crimea's `1939.1.1 = { buildings = { 3686 = { naval_facility = 1 } } }` (hoi4.exe
  // logs "Trying to set province building in state that doesn't own it" and skips it), 1032 - Yanan's dated
  // add_victory_points, Rise of Nations' dated set_province_name — 17 vanilla, 4 Novum Vexillum and 22 Rise of Nations
  // provinces, measured by erasing each. And the victory point went without the comment above it, which then captioned
  // the next one. A province that moves takes all of this with it (takeProvinceHistory); water has nowhere to take it,
  // so the same cut runs — every date, every kind, each with its comments — and the pieces are dropped.
  // ⛔ #an-erase-says-what-it-cut — …AND SAYS WHAT WENT. A victory point and a naval base went from the state's file with nothing said, on the
  // stroke's line or the Save's: Takibi's 8984 on Hearts of Minecraft (victory point 10, Byutushi, and a naval base of 3) and Litorale's
  // 6626 on the base game (3 and 5) (review of the T39 merge, S-erase-drops-vp-unsaid). `historyCut`, one entry a state, for the page's
  // erasedHistoryNote.
