    // its station: re-planned on TEST 37's own states, 14.4% of the track ran inside provinces over 1,000 px (the base game 4.2%), its
    // rail provinces were 1.10x as likely as its land to be that big (the base game 0.24x), and through-routes passed their station
    // by more than 10 px 114 times (the base game 15). So each border crossed costs RAIL_STEP_UNITS × the mean of its two provinces'
    // sizes, a size being √(px ÷ railProvinceMedianPxBeneath — vanilla 124) and never under one: a province no bigger than the rail
    // below's costs one step, as it did, and a sliver is no cheaper than a province (unfloored, a tie-break the walk's widest border
