    // soon as it was the cheapest, whatever its arrows did to the arrows already there, and on the walled-in islets of a generated
    // world TEST 32 (10-02) came out with 3 arrows within 1.5 px of a station they skip, 5 stations whose two arrows leave under 15
    // deg apart and 5 places where a row turns back under 20 deg — vanilla ships 0, 0 and 0. So each link the guards in the pass
    // let through is first asked of a ledger of every arrow drawn (railArrowLedger: a fan or a turn under RAIL_ARROW_FAN deg, or a
    // station on the rail within RAIL_ARROW_OVER px of an arrow that does not stop at it), seeded with every railway the game loads,
    // the layers below too, and growing with each row laid. One that would lie on them waits, and is laid after every other link of
    // its pass only if its two hubs are still apart: the pieces joined are the pieces they were, and what is laid instead is whatever
    // cheaper way was waiting behind it — usually the way through the station it would have skipped. It is asked between links, not
    // in the search (d, e): what it looks at is the rail earlier links laid. A crossing is not asked (railArrowLedger says why).
    // Re-planned on TEST 32's own 1,081 hubs: arrows within 2 px of a station they skip 4 → 1 (forced), fans under 15 deg 5 → 0,
    // turns under 20 deg 5 → 0, the narrowest fan 0.75 → 20.23 deg, 9 of 1,031 rows different, track +0.06%; on Millennium Dawn's
    // own hubs 3 → 1 over a station and 1 → 0 fans, Old World Blues' 16 → 4 and 6 → 0, TEST 31's fans 2 → 1 (forced); vanilla's,
    // Novum Vexillum's, Rise of Nations', Road to 56's and Hearts of Minecraft's byte-identical. The pieces, the hubs off the rail,
    // the hubs in the largest piece and the capitals' hubs on it are unchanged on every one, and no pair of hubs 40 px apart or less
    // is 20 rail hops further on any but Old World Blues (one: 137 → 376, a turn that waited) — what a wait can move and a piece
    // count cannot see. Rebuilt through the owner's flow (Delete map, Generate land 35% seed 1, Auto-fix, Redraw) on today's hubs:
