// ─── what a world is MADE OF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// ⛔ #a-generated-world-is-one-terrain — EVERY PROVINCE generateLand RAISED WAS `plains`.
//
// The writer below stamped `c[6] = "plains"` on every row it turned into land, so a world built through the
// owner's own sequence (new mod → Delete map → Generate land → Auto-fix) came out as ONE terrain type. That is
// two things at once: terrain.bmp paints what the row says, so the whole world is one ground texture; and
// terrain is what HOI4 reads for combat width, attack modifiers, movement cost, supply flow penalty and truck
// attrition, so every battle anywhere on it is fought on the same ground.
//
// 📊 NO SHIPPING MAP IS ONE TYPE. Land rows by terrain, measured over the six installed maps:
//
//     vanilla  plains 29.9%  forest 23.3%  mountain 16.8%  hills 13.3%  desert 8.0%  jungle 4.7%  urban 2.6%  marsh 1.4%
//     MD       plains 32.7%  forest 16.5%  mountain 16.0%  hills 11.5%  desert 9.7%  jungle 6.4%  urban 5.4%  marsh 1.4%
//     R56      plains 29.9%  forest 23.1%  mountain 17.8%  hills 12.7%  desert 7.7%  jungle 4.9%  urban 2.5%  marsh 1.3%
//     OWB      plains 41.7%  hills 18.4%   desert 18.3%    forest 8.8%  jungle 3.9%  urban 3.5%  mountain 3.3%  marsh 1.9%
//     NV       plains 26.2%  forest 21.1%  mountain 16.3%  urban 11.1%  hills 11.0%  desert 8.4%  jungle 4.7%  marsh 1.1%
//     RoN      plains 29.8%  forest 23.3%  mountain 16.8%  hills 13.3%  desert 8.2%  jungle 4.7%  urban 2.6%  marsh 1.4%
//
//     the owner's built world (flow7/world_b20)   plains 100.0% of 4,721
//
// ⭐ AND TERRAIN IS NOT SCATTERED — IT COMES IN PATCHES. The share of land-land province neighbour pairs that
// carry the SAME terrain, against the share independent draws from that same map's own mix would give:
//
//     vanilla 59.7% / 19.9%   MD 56.1% / 18.9%   R56 59.8% / 20.0%
//     OWB     73.5% / 25.3%   NV 55.8% / 17.4%   RoN 59.9% / 19.9%
