  // Nova's own wizard writes. ONE call flipped 10,154 land rows to sea and MATERIALISED six map files —
  // definition.csv (445 KB), heightmap.bmp (11.5 MB), a 0-byte supply_nodes.txt, a 0-byte railways.txt and
  // a 0-byte buildings.txt — while writing no provinces.bmp, no terrain.bmp and no rivers.bmp. It kept no
  // snapshot either: nothing was OVERWRITTEN, so snapshotFileBeforeOverwrite had nothing to copy and there
  // was nothing to restore from. 1,081 base states still loaded underneath, and 244 of vanilla's adjacency
  // rows still described land that was now sea.
