  // one prunes again: the last 200 survive and everything earlier in the SAME click is deleted.
  // Measured on the base commit, driving this function over mkdtemp copies of the installed corpus:
  //
  //     Millennium Dawn   394 backups taken, 200 left -> 194 evicted by the click itself
  //     Rise of Nations   492 backups taken, 200 left -> 292 evicted
  //
  // and in both the FIRST file written — map/definition.csv, which defines every province in the mod —
  // was no longer recoverable afterwards. Batch 12 removed the in-mod <file>.bak copy, so that pool is
  // now the only backup of an edited map file.
  //
  // The deletions below were already protected this way. This gives the OVERWRITES the same protection,
  // in the same timestamped folder, outside the mod and outside the prune pool. Copies only — nothing
