  // Nova has had three writers for map/rivers.bmp since long before this function existed — the river paint
  // tool, the clear-rivers tool and fixMalformedRivers — and the blank called none of them. So after the
  // owner's own sequence (own the map → Delete map → Generate land 35% → Auto-fix ×2) every river the base
  // game ever drew was still drawn, now over open ocean, and the new continents had none. The mod did not
  // even own rivers.bmp: it was vanilla's file, showing through the new world exactly as the terrain did
  // before batch 18 (#a-retyped-province-keeps-its-old-look — "weird things that looked like glass").
  //
  // 📊 Measured through this function on a scratch mod over the installed base game, 5,632×2,048:
  //
  //     before        90,353 river pixels — 88,174 over land · 1,549 over sea · 630 over lake, in 5,158 provinces
  //     after Delete  89,723 of those 90,353 (99.3%) stand over SEA, and 0 over land
  //     after Generate land 35%   53,959 (59.7%) still over sea, and 35,764 (39.6%) stranded on the NEW
  //                   continents — the drowned world's rivers, cut up and scattered across land they never
