  // land-with-no-sea, asked of every order of battle an event, focus or decision loads. A loaded fleet already at sea is
  // left out (a berth at sea loads, as above). Such a file names no country, so each unit is given the one it belongs to:
  //   a DIVISION, the country that held its province in the world the mod replaced — where the base game put it: 381 of
  //     vanilla's 381 loaded divisions stand on that country's 1936 land, though 230 of them belong to a country that owns
  //     nothing at the start (Slovakia on Czech land, the Cossack hosts on Soviet land). Its province is water now, and
  //     water has no owner, so the world below is the only one that can answer. Read only when one is found.
  //   a FLEET, the country that holds its province NOW: land with no sea is still land, and still somebody's. On Old World
  //     Blues the owner below (MEX) owns no harbour there and the owner now (SIN) is the one the file's ships name.
  // …the mod's own berths judged by its map alone here too (#a-berth-the-mods-own-file-gives-is-judged-by-the-map): Nova's fleet
