  // COPY, THE ONE NOVA READS. A copy that was not whole (it came out short, or the copy threw half-way) was left at its name, and in a
  // store kept by name that is the copy read FIRST: Restore answered "No saved removal found" while the whole archive sat in the mod, and
  // every later click kept it there, its name held. And the copy taken back after a failed unlink was taken back without asking whether
  // the file was still there: one an on-access scanner took away meanwhile (the unlink answers ENOENT) left that copy the ONLY one, and it
  // was deleted. So only this call's own copy is ever taken back, and only while the file it copies is still in the mod, untouched.
